<h1>Transposio – Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Developer: kgSoftwares · App ID: com.kgSoftwares.transposio · Last updated: 21 November 2026</p>

<p>Transposio changes the musical key of audio playing on your Android device. This policy
explains what data the app handles and why.</p>

<h2>Audio</h2>
<p>When you press Start, Transposio uses Android's audio-capture feature (shown by Android as
"screen sharing") to receive the sound that other apps are playing. The sound is
pitch-shifted in your device's memory and played back immediately. It is <strong>never
recorded, saved, or sent anywhere</strong>. Nothing on your screen is captured, and the
microphone is never used.</p>

<h2>Permissions</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Record audio / screen sharing:</strong> Android requires these for an app to receive
      other apps' sound. Used only while transposing is switched on.</li>
  <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> show the running notification with key and Stop controls.</li>
  <li><strong>Internet:</strong> used only to send anonymous usage statistics, and only if you allow
      them (see below).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Usage statistics (only with your consent)</h2>
<p>On first launch Transposio asks whether you allow anonymous usage statistics. Nothing is
collected unless you tap <strong>Allow</strong>. You can turn it off at any time with the switch at
the bottom of the app; turning it off also resets the analytics identifier.</p>
<p>If you allow it, Transposio uses <strong>Google Analytics for Firebase</strong> to understand how the
app is used and to fix problems. It collects:</p>
<ul>
  <li>App events: when transposing starts and stops, how long it ran, the semitones and cents
      used, whether sound was received, the detected musical key, and error messages.</li>
  <li>Standard device information: device model, Android version, app version, language, and
      approximate country (derived from the IP address, which is not stored).</li>
  <li>A random app-instance identifier.</li>
</ul>
<p>Transposio does <strong>not</strong> collect the advertising ID, your name, email, contacts, location,
files, or any audio, and does not use data for advertising.</p>

<h2>Who the data is shared with</h2>
<p>Usage statistics are processed by <strong>Google</strong> (Firebase / Google Analytics) as a service
provider on our behalf, under the
<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> and
<a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Firebase privacy terms</a>.
The data is not sold and not shared with anyone else.</p>

<h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>Event-level analytics data is kept for 2 months and then deleted automatically. Turning off
the switch in the app stops collection and resets the identifier. To ask for deletion of data
already collected, contact us at the address below.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>Data sent to Google Analytics is encrypted in transit (HTTPS).</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Transposio is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect their data.</p>

<h2>Volume</h2>
<p>While running, Transposio sets the media volume to 0 and plays the transposed sound on the
alarm volume, so that you hear only one song. Your previous volumes are restored when you press
Stop.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with a new date.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href="mailto:kgezerlissoftware@gmail.com">kgezerlissoftware@gmail.com</a></p>
</section>

